    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a team-high 81.88 efficiency score. The matchup against Scherzer is exceptionally favorable, as the veteran\u2019s high xERA of 5.10 provides the perfect runway for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.65) to exploit the lack of command. Both hitters benefit from the slow delivery of the opposition, which creates an underrated opportunity for stolen bases, a vital component of our strategy given the league\u2019s high premium on speed. Additionally, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (63.76) and **Jackson Merrill** (60.59) are set up for strong performances; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leverages a robust +14% platoon edge, while **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a helpful wind-out scenario that bolsters his floor despite a neutral park factor.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Wade Meckler** (38.82) on the bench. He narrowly missed the 40-point threshold, falling just short due to a stiff challenge from the opposing starter, Cavalli, whose 3.24 xERA stifled the overall projection. While **Wade Meckler** offered intrigue due to his batting order position, the decision to prioritize the efficiency of **Drake Baldwin** and **Coby Mayo**\u2014even with their own situational volatility\u2014was the safer play to preserve our game caps. Looking ahead, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages** on the IL, as their return remains critical to bolstering our late-season depth alongside prospects like **Nasim Nunez** and **Henry Bolte**. With **Kyle Tucker** (68.97) providing a reliable, high-floor anchor in the outfield, the Waves are well-positioned to maintain pressure in the standings, provided we avoid any late-breaking weather disruptions or unexpected lineup shifts affecting **Miguel Vargas** and the middle-order production.",
